Z||000000||turbo86se||03-29-2000||02:35 PM||||<BR>Well, I stopped by my mechanic's house to see what he was up to, and sitting out in front of his house is a nice white convertable 84. It's got IRM scoops on the sides, grey interior, grey leather seats, 169,000 fun-filled miles. NO A/C. I asked Mike why he had it after Mike said it ran great, he said he's converting the 4-spd into an automatic. The owner is getting old and it's getting hard for him to push in the clutch. I said sarcastically "I'll trade my 88 coupe for it!" (my 88 coupe is an auto). Mike called the owner and asked him what he thought, the owner said no, he is the original owner, and means too much to him (which I can understand). Oh well, would have been nice to have a convertable Fiero!!!||||reg||10
Z||000001||ChadMan||03-29-2000||02:41 PM||||Sounds like a nice car!  I met a woman who's a landlady/housemom on Otterbein College campus who has a beautiful silver 87 SE with a stuffed Garfield suction-cupped to the back glass.  She's past middle age but I wouldn't call her "old."  I asked her if she'd consider selling her Fiero and she said she'd never sell it - but "you can contact my estate when I'm gone and don't need it anymore.  But you've got a long wait!"<P>Stories like these make me think that maybe, just maybe, our little plastic Pontiacs will be worth some real money someday after all.||||reg||10
Z||000002||frontal lobe||03-29-2000||03:04 PM||||A STUFFED GARFIELD!!!!  I'm all for freedom of expression and individual liberty, but a suction-cupped stuffed Garfield????  At least show some class and have a bobbing-head chihuahua like me (I really don't have one, just kidding).  If you want to do that to a car, shouldn't it be a Ford Escort or something like that?||||reg||1
